The MIT terms above cover this repository's own files: the Chimera driver
and port layer (waterbox/), the patches (patches/), the tools and the
documents. They do not cover QUASI88, which this repository takes in as a
submodule (extern/QUASI88, https://github.com/bubio/QUASI88) and which the
built package (quasi88-<id>.chimeraCore) contains compiled. The package
holds, together:

- QUASI88 by Showzoh Fukunaga, in bubio's SDL2 port: BSD-3-Clause
  (extern/QUASI88/LICENSE).
- The sound drivers QUASI88 takes from MAME/XMAME
  (extern/QUASI88/src/snddrv/xmame): the old MAME licence
  (extern/QUASI88/src/snddrv/xmame/license.txt). It forbids selling the
  result or using it in a commercial product or activity, and asks that a
  modified build be distributed with its complete source.
- fmgen, cisc's FM sound generator (extern/QUASI88/src/snddrv/fmgen): the
  fmgen terms (extern/QUASI88/src/snddrv/fmgen/readme.txt). It may be
  modified and distributed freely if its origin is named, the result stays
  free software, changes are stated and its text is kept unchanged; putting
  it into commercial software needs its author's consent.

waterbox/package-licenses.json lists every part, and the package carries
each licence text.
